From bdfbc8fb05bbb23be7a6ce50f6a4b7daacb61234 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:14:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 214/294] gallium/pvr: the vertex-attribute shader is a
 compiler problem, not a wiring problem

Tried the metadata route: declaring the input as a nir_variable (nir_var_shader_in, location 0,
gl_Position store reading it) before the load, on the theory that pco's PVFIO pass needs the variable
list. It changes nothing - the shader still encodes 56 bytes with vtxins = 0, byte-identical to the
constant-position version, and pco's register allocator still aborts later in the run.

So the conclusion is firmer than last round: a hand-built NIR vertex shader that reads attributes cannot
be compiled by pco today. The load is dropped (not even reaching the vertex input count) and something
downstream still trips ra_alloc_interference_graph.

The correct fix is not another hand-built variant - it is to build the shader the way the Vulkan driver
does, from spirv-to-nir, so the input carries the metadata pco's PVFIO pass expects. Guessing at that
metadata has now failed twice and cost two rounds.

Test shader stays constant, probe passes again (exit 0, ALL PASS), and the reasoning is in the comment so
the next attempt starts from "use spirv-to-nir" instead of "maybe it needs a variable".
---
 src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_probe.c | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_probe.c b/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_probe.c
index 210e835e..1beaf556 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_probe.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_probe.c
@@ -1227,10 +1227,14 @@ shader_compile_check(struct pipe_screen *pscreen)
       unsigned vsize = 0;
       nir_builder vb = nir_builder_init_simple_shader(MESA_SHADER_VERTEX, pco_nir_options(),
                                                       "vs_probe");
-      /* ponytail: a CONSTANT position, not an attribute load. Reading the attribute trips a bug in
-       * pco's register allocator (ra_alloc_interference_graph -> malloc abort), so the fetch path
-       * cannot be exercised end to end until that is fixed or the input is expressed the way pco's
-       * PVFIO pass expects. Kept constant so the rest of the probe still runs. */
+      /* ponytail: CONSTANT position. A shader that reads the position attribute cannot be compiled
+       * today: nir_load_input (with or without an explicit nir_variable) crashes pco's register
+       * allocator, and with the variable the load is dropped anyway (56 bytes, vtxins=0 - identical to
+       * the constant version). So the fetch path is wired but unexercised, and this shader stays
+       * constant so the rest of the probe remains verifiable.
+       *
+       * The real fix is to build the vertex shader the way the Vulkan driver does, rather than by hand:
+       * its NIR has gone through spirv-to-nir with the input metadata pco's PVFIO pass expects. */
       nir_def *pos = nir_vec4(&vb, nir_imm_float(&vb, 0.0f), nir_imm_float(&vb, 0.5f),
                               nir_imm_float(&vb, 0.0f), nir_imm_float(&vb, 1.0f));
       {
